ion/pull/20564#discussion_r4264181151) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Disable metadata collection for setup-only trace-ID regression task](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20564#discussion_r4254055743)\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5510155922","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5510155922},{"body":"The stated Servlet/Tomcat cleanup is incomplete for the adjacent Tomcat 10 collection entries. `tomcat-10.0/javaagent/build.gradle.kts:30-32` still enables request-parameter capture for every test task, while lines 314-315 still collect the baseline and setup-only trace-ID variant. As a result, Tomcat 10 continues classifying captured request-parameter telemetry as default (and under the trace-ID label). Apply the same dedicated capture variant/default-off expectation there and stop collecting its trace-ID-only task.","comment_commit_id":"3fa15b0fb693877091bbf93e89d2346f8b1fc67e","comment_id":4264181151,"key":"inline:4264181151","kind":"inline","line":313,"original_commit_id":"3fa15b0fb693877091bbf93e89d2346f8b1fc67e","original_line":313,"path":".github/scripts/instrumentations.sh","review_commit_id":"3fa15b0fb693877091bbf93e89d2346f8b1fc67e","review_id":5510155922,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-13T21:24:30Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"